%N A400703 Numbers k whose trajectory under repeated application of the map x -> sigma(x) - x is not strictly decreasing.
%C A400703 Numbers for which the trajectory contains either a perfect or an abundant number.
%t A400703 q[k_] := NestWhile[DivisorSigma[1, #] - # &, k, #2 > 0 && #1 > #2 &, 2] > 0; Select[Range[158], q] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 04 2026 *)
%o A400703 (PARI) isok(k)=while(k, my(t=sigma(k)-k); if(t>=k,break); k=t); k!=0 \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 04 2026
%Y A400703 Cf. A000203 (sigma), A001065 (sum of all proper divisor).
%Y A400703 Cf. A005100, A005101 (abundant numbers, a subsequence), A000396 (perfect numbers, a subsequence).
%Y A400703 Cf. A023196 (either a perfect number or an abundant number, a subsequence).
%Y A400703 Cf. A003023, A080907, A126016.
